&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Artefact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a next-generation data and AI consulting firm dedicated to accelerating the adoption of data and AI to create measurable business impact across the full enterprise value chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We sit at the intersection of consulting, data science, AI technologies, data engineering, and digital transformation. We do not just advise — we build, implement, and deliver results our clients can measure. Our teams bring together consultants, data scientists, data engineers, AI engineers, analysts, and digital experts to solve complex business challenges with pragmatic, production-ready solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Artefact continues to grow globally, we are building a team of entrepreneurial data and AI talent who can help clients move beyond experimentation and into scalable, governed, value-generating AI adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is looking for a Senior Deployed AI Engineer specialized in Gemini Enterprise and the Google AI stack: an engineer who works embedded with our clients and takes AI products from idea to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design and build the interfaces, services, and agentic systems at the heart of our client work, such as conversational applications over enterprise data, multi-step agents that automate business workflows, and the retrieval and data pipelines that support them. You will own your components end to end: the front end, the service behind it, the data and retrieval pipelines feeding it, the deployment, and the evaluations proving it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines deep, certified expertise in Google&#39;s enterprise AI stack (Gemini models, Vertex AI, and the Gemini Enterprise agent platform) with the ability to deliver end to end. Beyond your platform specialization, you will be expected to work confidently across the full delivery lifecycle — full-stack development, data engineering, cloud infrastructure, evaluation, and client communication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with our clients, with direct exposure from the start, and you will support the professional development of the engineers around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Full-Stack AI Applications, End to End&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build AI products across the entire stack, from interface to infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop user-facing interfaces in TypeScript/React and the backend services and APIs behind them in Python or Node.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement agentic behavior: orchestration, tool and function calling, memory, and guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) pipelines: ingestion, chunking, embeddings, vector and hybrid search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect AI systems to enterprise data and applications via APIs, semantic layers, and protocols such as MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go Deep on Gemini Enterprise and the Google AI Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the team&#39;s reference for Google&#39;s enterprise AI platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build agents with Gemini models, Vertex AI, the Agent Development Kit (ADK), and Agent Engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and configure Gemini Enterprise for clients: Agent Designer for natural-language and trigger-based agents, the Inbox for managing long-running agents at scale, and agent sandboxes for autonomous problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect Gemini Enterprise to the client&#39;s application landscape through first-party and partner connectors, with proper permissions, governance, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build grounded, retrieval-backed applications with Vertex AI Search and RAG Engine, grounding with Google Search, and BigQuery as the data backbone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement agent interoperability through the A2A protocol and MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track Google&#39;s releases closely and translate new capabilities into client value quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make AI Systems Production-Grade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our standard is production quality: systems that are reliable, monitored, and maintainable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write evaluation suites and regression tests for LLM-powered features, and monitor cost, latency, and quality in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply solid engineering practice: version control, code review, automated testing, CI/CD, and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy on cloud infrastructure (GCP, Azure, or AWS) using containers, serverless, and infrastructure-as-code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the data pipelines that feed AI systems, across warehouses, lakehouses, and vector stores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work AI-Natively and Client-Facing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our engineers work AI-natively and represent Artefact directly with clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex, Cursor) daily, with good judgment about verification and review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate progress, trade-offs, and blockers clearly to clients and project leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pre-sales when needed: scope solutions, build demos, and estimate effort with our partnership and consulting teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior engineers and contribute to internal accelerators, reusable components, and engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in software engineering or data engineering, with extensive hands-on use of AI tools and LLM-based development over the past year (professional projects, internal initiatives, or substantial personal builds).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience with the Google AI stack: Gemini models, Vertex AI, and ideally Gemini Enterprise or ADK — ideally with experience taking at least one solution to production on GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python and TypeScript/JavaScript, and experience building and consuming APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with front-end development (React or similar) and at least one backend framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with RAG, embeddings, and vector search, and with at least one agentic framework (Google ADK, LangGraph/LangChain).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working experience with GCP; Azure or AWS is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with agentic coding tools such as Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex, or Cursor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in computer science, engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Google Cloud certification is a strong differentiator at application. If you do not hold one yet, obtaining it within your first 2 months in the role is a requirement — Artefact sponsors the exam and gives you time to prepare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Cloud Professional Machine Learning Engineer (preferred), covering Vertex AI, generative AI, and production ML.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Cloud Generative AI Leader is valued as a foundation, complemented by hands-on Vertex AI / Gemini Enterprise delivery experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MCP servers, multi-agent patterns, or LLM evaluation tooling (LangSmith, Langfuse, promptfoo).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Terraform or CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GCP, BigQuery, or Google Workspace integrations alongside Gemini Enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong candidate will bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Gemini Enterprise and the Google AI stack, combined with breadth across the full stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns features end to end, from interface to infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cares about evaluation and reliability, not just the happy path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates clearly with clients in demos, documents, and code review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-facing mindset: understands client needs and translates business requirements into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learns new tools and models fast, and shares what works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Artefact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Artefact, data and AI are not abstract strategy topics. They are tools for creating business value, improving organizations, and helping people make better decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a global community of data and AI experts who combine consulting, engineering, data science, marketing, and technology expertise. You will work on complex, high-impact problems with leading organizations and help shape how enterprises adopt AI responsibly and effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value action, collaboration, learning, client trust, and shared knowledge. We believe that technology only matters when it is used, adopted, and translated into impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our values aren&#39;t decorations on a wall — they&#39;re how we actually work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There is always a way&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— We&#39;re builders and problem-solvers. An idea only counts if it gets executed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client trust is won in the field&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— We show up, sleeves rolled up, working side by side with our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If it&#39;s not used, it&#39;s useless&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— We build for adoption and impact, not for slide decks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If it&#39;s not shared, we&#39;re not done&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— Knowledge shared compounds. We invest in each other&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We learn every day&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— In a field that moves this fast, standing still means falling behind. We embrace the challenge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Paid Social Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is looking for an experienced Senior Paid Social Account Manager to take senior ownership of paid social activity across two key client accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role combining account strategy, technical auditing, campaign management, optimisation, performance analysis and senior client management. The successful candidate will be expected to understand the detail of platform execution while also providing clear strategic direction and identifying opportunities to grow client performance and the wider relationship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Meta expertise is essential. The person should be able to inherit an existing account, independently assess whether the setup is technically and strategically sound, identify weaknesses or missed opportunities, prioritise improvements and lead their implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will initially focus on two clients, allowing the Senior Paid Social Account Manager to build a deep understanding of their businesses, act as a trusted paid social adviser and take genuine accountability for account quality and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account leadership and client strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior day-to-day paid social lead for the assigned clients, owning the relationship for the channel and ensuring consistently high-quality delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of each client’s business model, commercial priorities, customer journey and wider media strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business objectives into clear paid social strategies, investment recommendations, testing roadmaps and activation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present strategic recommendations, performance insights and account priorities confidently to senior client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge existing approaches constructively and proactively identify opportunities to improve performance or expand the role of paid social.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Search, Programmatic, Retail Media, Commerce, Influencer, Creative and Data teams to provide integrated recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual, quarterly and campaign-level planning, including budget allocation, forecasting and scenario planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meta account audits and technical setup&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A core part of the role will be independently assessing whether existing Meta environments are correctly structured for activation, optimisation and measurement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Portfolio / Business Manager setup, permissions and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ad account structure and campaign architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain, page, Instagram and other asset configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meta Pixel, Conversions API, events and conversion optimisation setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data quality, event match quality and potential tracking gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product catalogues, feeds and commerce integrations where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audience strategy, exclusions and first-party data activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budget, bidding and optimisation configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attribution and measurement settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Naming conventions, campaign taxonomy and account governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative, placement and format setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account-level automated settings and relevant platform recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration with analytics, ecommerce and measurement environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Paid Social Account Manager should be able to document audit findings clearly, distinguish critical issues from lower-priority improvements, build an action plan and either implement or coordinate the required changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid social strategy and planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop paid social strategies aligned with client business, media and commercial objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the role of different paid social platforms, audiences, creative formats and campaign objectives within the wider media mix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build structured testing roadmaps covering audiences, creative, formats, placements, bidding and new platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend how paid social should work alongside influencer and creator activity, including paid amplification of creator content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve incrementality, efficiency and scale rather than focusing solely on platform-reported performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear recommendations on where investment should be increased, reduced or reallocated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign management and optimisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retain sufficient hands-on involvement to understand account performance and ensure execution remains strong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee campaign setup, structures, audiences, bidding, budgets, placements and creative deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure campaigns are launched accurately and on time, with appropriate QA and measurement foundations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor pacing and performance against agreed objectives and proactively identify issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead optimisation decisions and ensure actions are based on evidence rather than routine platform changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong account hygiene, documentation and platform best practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review work completed by more junior team members where relevant and provide clear guidance and quality control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meta&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced hands-on Meta experience is essential. The successful candidate should be highly confident across:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meta Ads Manager and Business Portfolio / Business Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Campaign architecture and account restructuring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audience strategy and first-party data activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantage+ solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversion, catalogue and ecommerce campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative testing and Reels/video formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership Ads and creator-led paid amplification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pixel, Conversions API, events and conversion optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product catalogues and feeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budget and bidding strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attribution, measurement and experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account troubleshooting, audits and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The person should be comfortable inheriting an account they have never seen before and quickly determining whether the foundations are strong, what is limiting performance and whether restructuring is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TikTok&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong TikTok Ads experience is highly desirable, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Campaign setup, optimisation and account structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spark Ads and creator-led paid amplification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audience and creative testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance analysis and budget optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how paid media can connect with TikTok Shop activity where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other platforms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with additional paid social environments is beneficial, particularly:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LinkedIn Campaign Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pinterest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;YouTube / Google video environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emerging social and creator-led advertising platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate does not need equal expertise across every platform, but should be curious, adaptable and able to expand into new environments as client needs evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance, measurement and insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse performance across campaigns, audiences, creatives, placements and conversion journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain the drivers behind performance changes rather than simply report results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate platform metrics into clear commercial implications and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with analytics specialists where deeper measurement support is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support experimentation, incrementality, attribution and other measurement initiatives where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure reporting focuses on decisions and next actions, not only retrospective performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate budget tracking, campaign documentation and key account-change records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creative and creator collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Paid social performance increasingly depends on creative quality. The role will therefore work closely with clients, creative teams and influencer specialists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop creative testing frameworks and identify high-performing themes, formats and messages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate campaign data into actionable creative recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on platform-specific creative best practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to use influencer and creator content within paid campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend opportunities for Spark Ads, Partnership Ads and other creator-led formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed paid-media learnings back into future content and creator planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial ownership and capability development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Client delivery is the core responsibility, but at Senior Account Manager level we also expect the person to contribute to account growth and the wider development of Artefact’s paid social capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify growth opportunities within existing client accounts and turn them into clear recommendations or proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot relevant cross-sell opportunities across media, commerce, influencer and measurement capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pitches, new-business proposals and client growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop a repeatable Meta audit framework and paid social best-practice standards for the wider team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with Meta, TikTok and other relevant platform partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to new platform products, betas and market developments and assess their relevance for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop case studies, training materials and internal knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to improving paid social processes, governance and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team contribution and mentoring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance, QA and coaching to more junior paid media team members where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help raise the overall standard of paid social knowledge across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delegate appropriately while remaining accountable for the quality of client output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an environment where issues are identified early and recommendations are proactive rather than reactive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on paid social experience, ideally within an agency or multi-client environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Meta Ads expertise and confidence operating at both strategic and technical levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience auditing existing Meta accounts and identifying setup, tracking, structure and optimisation issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently assess whether an account is correctly configured and prioritise the required changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Meta Pixel, Conversions API, events and conversion measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience restructuring or materially improving existing accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong campaign-management, optimisation and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing audience, creative and campaign testing strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex performance data into clear strategic and commercial recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong client-management skills and confidence presenting to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking ownership of multiple workstreams and priorities across client accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, accountability and a proactive approach to identifying problems and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial mindset and willingness to contribute to account growth and new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on TikTok Ads experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ecommerce and catalogue-based Meta activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with creator-led paid media, including Spark Ads and Meta Partnership Ads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with retail, ecommerce or consumer brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of product feeds and catalogue management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside influencer, retail-media or commerce teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with experimentation, attribution and incrementality measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience participating in pitches, proposals or account-growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or reviewing the work of more junior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LinkedIn Ads experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pinterest experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TikTok Shop knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Analytics / GA4 knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Looker Studio or similar reporting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple European markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the first few months, we would expect this person to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently audit both client Meta environments and clearly prioritise the changes required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take senior ownership of paid social strategy and ongoing activation across both accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with client stakeholders and become the go-to paid social adviser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve performance through structured optimisation, experimentation and stronger creative insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong account, tracking and measurement foundations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring proactive recommendations and growth opportunities rather than waiting for client requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect paid social more effectively with creative, influencer, commerce and wider media activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise delivery standards through strong QA, documentation and guidance to other team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of Artefact’s paid social capability and commercial growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is an applied AI company. We build systems that run in production, in our clients&#39; own cloud, and keep running after we leave. We are present in 27 countries across all continents with a team of 2,500 employees, offering a comprehensive set of AI &amp;amp; data solutions built on deep data science and cutting-edge AI technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From strategy to operations, we partner with 1,000+ clients, including some of the world’s top 300 brands such as Samsung, L’Oréal and Sanofi. Our work spans the full data and AI value chain, including data strategy, data quality and governance, data platforms, AI solutions, and data-driven customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact Benelux is looking for an ambitious Senior Programmatic Display Consultant to shape the future of our programmatic display &amp;amp; video offering from our Utrecht office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join our growing 15-person Digital &amp;amp; Data Marketing team and play a key part in our Programmatic Display &amp;amp; Video team. Together, we deliver best-in-class media strategy, audience management and innovative campaigns across display and video platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll drive branding and performance results for national and international clients, working closely with the paid media team and client strategists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a local Google Marketing Platform (GMP) reseller, we have a strong relationship with Google and deep knowledge of its tech stack. We don’t just run exceptional campaigns: we also onboard clients onto GMP, advise on best-in-class setup, media and audience strategy, and support their in-house teams along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also work with local publishers and other programmatic solutions. Artefact is tool- and publisher-agnostic, and always looks for the best results for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate client objectives into communication and online marketing strategy, including media mix, KPI setting and media plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement and optimize programmatic display and video strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee day-to-day campaign management and act as the main point of contact for your clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client relationships, from client-facing communication to ongoing account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with DSPs such as DV360 and publishers such as DPG, ShowHeroes and GumGum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build new partnerships with publishers active in the Benelux market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard clients onto Google Marketing Platform, supporting account creation and integration into their wider digital ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are analytical, detail-oriented and curious. You take ownership, learn new tools independently, and aren’t afraid to challenge existing ways of working. On top of that, you bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years of experience in a similar role, ideally at an online advertising agency or advertiser&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent Dutch and English&lt;/li&gt;
